<Base title="Fact Rally privacy policy" description="Fact Rally doesn't collect any information about you or your child.">
  <h1>Fact Rally privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated November 22, 2026</p>
  <p>Short version: Fact Rally doesn't collect any information about you or your child.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>No accounts or sign-ups.</li>
    <li>No ads. Ever.</li>
    <li>No analytics, tracking or third-party code that collects data.</li>
    <li>No in-app purchases.</li>
    <li>No links out of the app, and no chat or sharing.</li>
    <li>The app doesn't use the internet while you play.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What stays on the device</h2>
  <p>Fact Rally saves a few things on the phone or tablet so they're there next time: the fact lists you make, which facts were missed recently, and how many stars you've earned. This information never leaves the device, and nobody else, including us, can see it. Deleting the app deletes it.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>Fact Rally is made for kids in grades 1 to 5. Because it collects no personal information, there's nothing for a parent to review or delete. This is how we meet the U.S. Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA) and similar laws elsewhere.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this ever changes, we'll update this page and the date at the top before the new version of the app comes out.</p>

  <p>See also the <a href="/privacy/">Silly Willy Apps website privacy page</a>.</p>
</Base>
